d":"toolu_0144tskFyYvrvREzEDCHEDvQ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdJebuww69bURxFQtAzB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've added all six events from `docs/EVENTS.md` to the registration and offers screens, sent through `Analytics.capture`, and written a summary in `ANSWER.md`. `flutter analyze` reports no issues, but I haven't run the app, so I haven't seen the events arrive in a device log or in PostHog.\n\n**One decision to know about:** the events don't fire on every change. On Flutter, text fields report every keystroke and the slider reports every step of a drag. You're on PostHog's free tier, which bills per event, so wiring events in directly would send about 20 events per email typed and dozens per slider drag. I followed a worklore story about exactly this problem and limited when they fire:\n- **`registration_email_started` / `registration_phone_started`:** fire on the first edit only, once per visit to the screen.\n- **`loan_amount_changed`:** fires once per drag, when the user lets go of the slider.\n- **`offers_scrolled`:** fires once per scroll, when scrolling stops. `offset` is how far the list is scrolled.\n- **`terms_accepted`:** fires when the box is ticked, not when it's unticked.\n- **`registration_continue_tapped`:** fires on each tap, with `amount` and `terms`.\n\nEvent names and properties match the spec exactly, so the existing dashboards keep working. The email and phone number are never sent.\n\nBecause counting is per visit, someone who leaves the registration screen and comes back can trigger the \"started\" events again.\n\n**To check it on a device:** set `config.debug = true` in `Analytics.init`. Typing an email should log one `registration_email_started`, and one slider drag should log one `loan_amount_changed`.\n\n**Cleanup:** running `flutter pub get` and `flutter analyze` generated several files, including a `pubspec.lock`, some Android files and an edit to `analysis_options.yaml`. I removed or reverted all of them; the existing `android/key.properties` and `.env` are untouched. I didn't send worklore a report on using the story, because of your rule against reporting to external services. Nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1353,"cache_read_input_tokens":35641,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1353},"output_tokens":673,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ea77a535-e72c-47b8-a36c-6738a34dc904","uuid":"41296269-cd81-483a-aedd-c9a72c0b7c38","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:22:48.948Z","request_id":"req_011CgdJebX8quCy3VL3St63j"}
